# Scrape pipeline

Spiders yield `ContentItem` records ([`ntn_scraper/items.py`](ntn_scraper/items.py)). Pipeline writes JSON + Markdown bodies.

## ContentItem fields

Required: `id`, `type`, `source_url`, `title`, `region`, `language`, `body_html`, `body_markdown`, `images`, `scraped_at`.

Types → files: `page` → `pages.json`, `people` → `people.json`, `article` → `articles.json`, `thought` → `thoughts.json`, `testimonial` → `testimonials.json`, `course` → `courses_current.json`.

## Merge behaviour

Re-scraping **merges by `id`** into existing JSON — updates records, does not duplicate. Markdown mirrors: `data/bodies/{id}.md` with YAML front matter.

## Spiders

| Spider | Command | Source |
|--------|---------|--------|
| `legacy` | `scrapy crawl legacy` | Dreamweaver `.htm` pages |
| `wordpress` | `scrapy crawl wordpress` | WP REST API |
| `courses` | `scrapy crawl courses` | UK Events Manager HTML |

Run all: `./scripts/scrape_all.sh`

## Example: edit raw content without re-scraping

Edit `data/bodies/approach.md` or the matching record in `data/pages.json`, then run `python scripts/build_web.py` (Stage 3 only).

